causes.fix:
Check the blade and jamb seals and the actuator's closed-position torque (it must compress the seals);
replace seals or blades; add a tight-shutoff low-leak damper ahead of the old one; confirm the spring
return closes on power loss; keep the coil circulating through shutdowns.

causes.confirm:
Outdoor coil is below 25 °F and iced solid, but the snap-disc defrost thermostat reads open (or the NTC
thermistor reads a warm resistance, or the ambient sensor on a demand-defrost board reads off the curve);
jumping the sensor terminals and TEST pins immediately starts defrost.

causes.fix:
Check the cooling valve's command first — a controller calling both valves open is a control fault, not a
valve fault. If the command is closed, check the actuator for a manual-open setting, then the valve seat;
replace the cartridge or valve if it leaks through. A 4-pipe unit should never have both valves open at once.
